num values. Omit it to get the index of pages.", "enum": ["github.access", "connectors.add", "connectors.tool_off", "environment.secrets", "environment.network", "environment.dependencies", "environment.setup_script", "session.resources", "session.permissions", "remote_control.setup"], "type": "string"}}, "required": [], "type": "object"}, "name": "mcp__claude-code-remote__read_documentation"}, "server": "claude-code-remote"}, {"description": "Tell the session that a repo attached via add_repo has finished cloning, so its CLAUDE.md, skills, and plugins load on the next turn. Only call this immediately after a successful clone that add_repo instructed you to run — it returns a tool error for a repo that is not already in this session's sources.", "name": "mcp__claude-code-remote__register_repo_root", "schema": {"description": "Tell the session that a repo attached via add_repo has finished cloning, so its CLAUDE.md, skills, and plugins load on the next turn. Only call this immediately after a successful clone that add_repo instructed you to run — it returns a tool error for a repo that is not already in this session's sources.", "eager_input_streaming": true, "input_schema": {"properties": {"directory": {"description": "Absolute path of the clone on disk. Pass the real path you cloned to; on a self-hosted runner this will be under the session's base working directory.", "type": "string"}, "owner": {"description": "GitHub owner of the repo that was just cloned (same value passed to add_repo).", "type": "string"}, "repo": {"description": "GitHub repo name that was just cloned (same value passed to add_repo).", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["owner", "repo"], "type": "object"}, "name": "mcp__claude-code-remote__register_repo_root"}, "server": "claude-code-remote"}, {"description": "Tell the person's app which port on this session's machine serves a web page they may want to look at. The person may be following this session from a phone or a browser, where a preview pane can show that page. The app does not know the port unless you say so.\n\n- Call this when a dev server or other web server is up and the person may want to see its page, or when you are about to point them to one that was already running. Give the port it really listens on: read it from the server's output, not from what you asked for, since many servers move to the next free port.\n- Call it once for each server, and again only if that server's port changes. A restart on the same port needs no new call.\n- When more than one server runs, give each a short name, such as \"web\" or \"docs\".\n- Do not call it for a database, a debugger, an API with no page, a port nothing listens on, or a server you start only for your own tests.\n- This tool only states the port: it starts nothing and opens nothing. The app decides what to show and the person decides whether to open it. Not every app shows a preview, so do not tell the person one is ready because you called this.\n- If a tool whose name ends in preview_start started the server, that call already gave the port, so do not call this tool for that server.", "name": "mcp__claude-code-remote__report_preview_port", "schema": {"description": "Tell the person's app which port on this session's machine serves a web page they may want to look at. The person may be following this session from a phone or a browser, where a preview pane can show that page. The app does not know the port unless you say so.\n\n- Call this when a dev server or other web server is up and the person may want to see its page, or when you are about to point them to one that was already running. Give the port it really listens on: read it from the server's output, not from what you asked for, since many servers move to the next free port.\n- Call it once for each server, and again only if that server's port changes. A restart on the same port needs no new call.\n- When more than one server runs, give each a short name, such as \"web\" or \"docs\".\n- 